[33mcommit d267c512765516151b85944ba42d860f8b407273[m
Author: Thierry Ducrest <thierry.ducrest@camptocamp.com>
Date:   Tue Sep 7 13:19:32 2021 +0200

    Fix not split picking on scheduled date set in the past
    
    When the date_planned of the purchase order line is moved in the future
    the scheduled date of the picking is not changed by the `super` call of
    the `write` function.
    But when the date_planned is moved in the past the scheduled date
    of the picking is changed to the new date_planned.
    
    This is happening because the `scheduled_date` on the stock.picking is
    computed and the oldest `date_expected` of the related stock.moves is
    set as `scheduled_date`.
    
    https://github.com/odoo/odoo/blob/b53d36b8c4f6afd44b884f6acea9a222ff79b52d/addons/stock/models/stock_picking.py#L464
    
    This change fixes the problem, by not accepting a picking as valid if it
    has multiple date planned set on the stock.moves

